{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/662066-scion-in-other-systems","id":662066,"title":"Scion in other Systems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-12T11:40:23-07:00","id":662066,"title":"Scion in other Systems","content":"While it has its own system, there has always been talk of fixes and issues. So I wonder have any of you used the Scion setting with a different gaming system and how did it turn out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T17:05:32-07:00","id":662421,"title":"","content":"It wasn't technically Scion; but I've used Scion's material to flesh out the Ethereal Gods of In Nomine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T23:50:21-07:00","id":662735,"title":"","content":"Part-Time Gods (Though I used the FATE-hack version).<br /> Worlds in Peril<br /> <br /> Both of these systems push hard on the theme of balancing humanity with power, to the point of game mechanics, not just themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T05:37:10-07:00","id":662986,"title":"","content":"It also works pretty well in Mutants and Masterminds. Especially for the theme of 'no two scions doing the same thing in the same way'. You can have two scions of, say, water deities with very different powers in their water arrays. Even if they have the same parent. It's a fairly rules light, easy-to-adventure system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T09:37:08-07:00","id":663231,"title":"","content":"Part-Time Gods sounds right although I haven't looked at the Fate version as of yet.<br /> <br /> And anything super hero based is about what I expected. I have of late been considering trying to do Scion with the super hero twist on the Cipher System.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-18T22:08:00-07:00","id":670484,"title":"","content":"I read a story based on a gaming sessions in which Scion crossed over with Masquerade. A newly ascended sun goddess crash lands into a building where the Camarilla are being attacked by Sabbat. She flips the switch and vaporizes them on the spot before leaving. The Camarilla being understandably terrified of her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T11:29:30-07:00","id":671159,"title":"","content":"Right when Scion came out I was trying to convince my group to play. They were leery about it and wanted to play Feng Shui so I ran a game where they were each a scion of one of the Four Monarchs. We used Itztli as their pantheonic purview to represent what the Feng Shui sites were supposed to give you. It was a short game but it was fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T05:09:38-07:00","id":671822,"title":"","content":"Once did a discussion Hunter: the Vigil forums about Taskforce: Valkyrie's sometimes obsessive of norse mythology in their nomenclature and as connections and the occasional hint of occult lore were brought up one thing lead to another and the topic evolved into the sketch of a campaign, the Collection of Heroes, centered in the idea of how the TF:V's &quot;special identification circuits&quot; were actually runes that marked hunters and how those made themselves into worthy heroes through their battles with the supernatural, to be collected upon death for Valhalla. From there things simply evolved into a &quot;Scion:Ragnarok in nWoD&quot; kind of saga, one that i unfortunately have no idea if any of the people involved in the discussion ever STed.<br /> <br /> Scion were to be portrayed with the &quot;dark heroes&quot; from Mirrors as expies and as the deities as presented in Scion still felt all too human when compared to the sheer alien weirdness of the typical nWoD spirit, a dark hero-purified (from Immortals) combo was to be used for the gods themselves to explain that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}